  "asset_prompts": [
    "A hand-drawn black marker doodle explainer illustration on off-white paper,\nvertical infographic with 4 stacked panels separated by thin hand-drawn lines.\n\nCharacter: a simple solid-black round blob person with two white dot eyes,\na small curved smile, and thin black stick arms and legs. The body is solid\nflat black with smooth edges (no sketchy texture). The SAME character appears\nin every panel doing a different action.\n\nStyle: clean black marker/pen outlines, slightly wobbly but fully closed\nhand-drawn lines. All objects are OUTLINE-ONLY black line-art with white\ninteriors, no shading, no fill. Everything is monochrome black & white EXCEPT\none orange accent color used ONLY for the single key item in each panel.\nHand-drawn curved arrows in red or blue point at key spots, each with a short\nhandwritten Chinese label. Each panel has a bold hand-written marker-style\nChinese title at the top. Minimalist composition, lots of white space.\n\nPanels:\n1. A bean presenter stands on the LEFT, holding an orange umbrella tilted against curved wind lines. On the RIGHT a cyclone spiral is offshore, not above the presenter. Rain streaks above umbrella. No letters or numbers.\n2. A bean presenter on the LEFT points toward a large cyclone swirl on the RIGHT. The cyclone has a small orange center dot and much wider surrounding spiral bands. Show visibly that the storm extends well beyond its center. No letters or numbers.\n3. A bean presenter on the LEFT gestures to a large simple circle on the RIGHT. The circle has an orange center dot and an orange straight radius segment from that center to the right circumference. Keep the radius exact and connected to both center and boundary. No letters or numbers.\n4. A bean presenter on the LEFT stays inside a simple outline house, visible through the large open doorway. On the RIGHT, a spiral storm with outer curved rain bands; one rain band extends toward the house. Small orange warning triangle above the house. No letters or numbers.\nProduction content instruction: Keep all Chinese title and arrow-label positions EMPTY for separately editable typography. Four equally tall stacked panels, each with generous white margins; no panel numbers or text. Keep presenter at x15–35% and diagram at x50–88% in every panel. This is a schematic educational drawing, not a forecast for a real storm."
  ]
